EXT. ABANDONED DRIVE-IN SCREEN, ROOFTOP OF THE CONCESSION STAND - NIGHT

A cracked concrete rooftop under a vast, wheeling sky. Below, the lot is a field of rusted speaker posts. Above them, the screen towers, blank and enormous, a white rectangle hung against the stars.

Four teenagers sprawl on the tar paper with a cooler and a boombox playing something tinny and joyous.

JUNIPER "JUNE" OKAFOR-LINDQVIST (17, scraped knees, a purple streak in her hair) balances on the parapet with her arms out like wings. DEXTER "DEX" ALVARADO-CHEN (18, glasses, a sunburn in the shape of a watch) sits cross-legged, aiming a laser pointer at the screen. MAEVE O'DONNELL-BASU (17, a denim jacket three sizes too big) drums a beat on the cooler. And ANSEL REYNOLDS (18, a letterman jacket without a letter) lies flat on his back, eyes closed, a grin spreading slowly across his face.

JUNE
(to everyone)
We are the last people on Earth!

DEX
(to June)
You're going to fall.

JUNE
I'm going to fly.

MAEVE
(to herself)
Please don't fly.

ANSEL
(eyes closed)
Everyone shut up. This is the best night of my life.

DEX
You said that last week.

ANSEL
It was true last week too.

The laser dot dances across the white screen, a red comet looping among the stars. June leaps from the parapet to the roof, landing in a crouch, whooping.

JUNE
Nobody's ever going to know we were here!

MAEVE
(to Dex)
Is that supposed to be sad?

DEX
(to Maeve)
No. I think it's the opposite.

June grabs Maeve's hands and spins her. The boombox swells. Ansel sits up, laughing, and throws a can of soda. Dex ducks. It bursts against the screen's concrete foot below, a tiny sticky firework.

ANSEL
Direct hit!

MAEVE
(to the sky)
Please never end.

DEX
(to all of them)
It won't, not for us.

They fall quiet, laughing still, panting, four small figures on a roof beneath the enormous empty screen.
